    "summary": "I built a single-cell storage box with a magnetic lid. It's one full hex base with solid end caps on all six side faces, closed by a full cover on top. The cover sits on 3 snaps. The magnets were already switched on for the cover: when I tried to turn them on, the configurator said that changed nothing. The parts list includes 6 Ø5×1 mm neodymium magnets and 6 copper-coated 4.5 mm steel BBs. The box has 11 printed parts, about 481 g of filament and about 686 minutes of printing. check_build found no rule issues, and its mesh check came back \"clear\". Locking the joints changed nothing, because a single cell has no joints between cells to bolt. The configurator only checks fit and collisions, so how strongly the magnets hold the lid shut hasn't been tested.",
    "outcome": "built"
  },
